{"_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "lesson_name", "content": ""}, {"type": "unit_name", "content": "Data Validation"}, {"type": "position", "content": 7}, {"type": "origin", "content": "stub"}, {"type": "lesson", "content": 2}, {"type": "level", "content": "B1.1"}], "type": "metadata"}, {"contents": [{"type": "test", "content": "false"}], "type": "achievment_test"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "These are words you use when  talking about data validation. "}], "type": "target_word_describer"}, {"contents": [{"type": "primary", "content": "Designs the data structure based on the database structures and its characteristics. Validates database using the proper IT tools."}, {"type": "secondary_1", "content": "Discusses a range of options for potential actions at work through the correct use of grammar, vocabulary; level of formality and purpose, and cohesion and coherence aspects appropriate to this level.  Exchanges simple information on the data validation and data warehouses."}], "type": "objectives"}, {"type": "background_image", "content": "enpe8n5le02ob07re1img01.jpg"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Would Rather for What Is Preferable Negative Form"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "You use the expression <strong>would rather</strong> to show preference.   "}, {"type": "example", "content": "I'd rather not look at the time."}, {"type": "text", "content": "The expression <strong>would rather</strong> in negative form can be used to show preference of one negative option over several. Remember that you can use the abbreviation of would, which is \u201c 'd\u201d.  The structure that you have to follow in order to create negative sentences using this expression is:  <br/><br/> Subject + <strong>would rather</strong> + not + verb (base form) + complement. <br/><br/><span class=\"italic\"> For example:  I <span class=\"strong\">would rather not</span> continue working for this software company.  </span> <br/> After a request, you can also use this expression as an equivalent of  I <span class=\"strong\">don't want to</span>. <br/><br/> <span class=\"italic\"> For example:  Joseph: I want you to tell me about the company's crisis.<br/> Andrea: I<span class=\"strong\">'d rather not talk </span> about that.  </span>"}, {"type": "example", "content": "I'd rather not look at the time."}, {"type": "example", "content": "I would rather not be so specific about that."}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Different Options to Perform a Data Validation"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "Data validation, the process in which you make sure that the system's input is correct, accurate and fully operational, can be made taking into account different options. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "In any type of validation, the database that is being validated has to shut down in order to avoid any other users to access the system. Additionally, any type of validation must check and fix the following aspects: <br/><br/>  -\tOrphan pages <br/>-\tReport of misallocated pages <br/>-\tFaulty data structures <br/><br/>  Look at the following chart to know more about the different options to perform data validations. "}, {"type": "table", "content": "{\"rows\":5,\"columns\":3,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div class=\\\"center_text\\\"> Data validation option</div>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div class=\\\"center_text\\\">Description</div>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div class=\\\"center_text\\\">Command</div>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Default Validation\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"This validation option identifies orphan pages and updates them. At the end, this option updates the system and repairs corrupted structures. \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"gfix -v[alidate] database_name\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Full Validation\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"This validation option confirms, reports and updates any type of corrupted structures in both page and record levels. \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"gfix -v[alidate] -full database_name\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Read-only Validation\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"This validation type does not make any changes to the database that is being checked. It only reports all the different areas that show inconsistencies or problems. \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"gfix -v[alidate] -full -n[o_update] database_name\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Ignore Checksum Error\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"The validation of the data in a page is confirmed by checksums. In fact, ignoring checksum errors enables the validation of corrupted databases; furthermore, the data recovered by this option will no longer be useful. \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"gfix -v[alidate] -full -i[gnore] -n[o_update] database_name\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border instruction_table_background\"}"}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "suitably"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "in a correct and appropriate way or manner "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adverb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: I would rather not see it as a validation but as an inspection of the data needed for the system to perform suitably."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n5le02ob07aud01"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "in accordance with "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "obeying or following something "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(expression)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: This process makes sure that the different inputs of the system work in accordance with their purpose."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n5le02ob07aud02"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "execute "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to carry out something, to perform an action or activity "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Furthermore, we would rather not execute it when the application is finished, but throughout its development stage. "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n5le02ob07aud03"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "aim "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to intend to achieve or accomplish something "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Sure, the data validation is going to aim to verify the completeness and correctness of all the data needed in the application."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n5le02ob07aud04"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "orphan page"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a page that is intended to function, but that ends up failing and being unused"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": " Example: The default validation, which identifies orphan pages and updates them."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n5le02ob07aud05"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "corrupt "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "information that is not usable as it changes and fails "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Finally, the ignore checksum error enables the validation of corrupted databases. "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n5le02ob07aud06"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "Look for information about validation of new software in companies. \t"}, {"type": "text", "conte