erride": 1, "questions": [{"_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "pdf", "content": "enpe8n5le02ob07re7pdf01.pdf"}], "type": "question"}], "responses": [{"_data": [{"type": "text", "content": ""}], "selected": 0, "correct": 1, "id": 0}], "id": 0}], "type": "DWS", "_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "Let's evaluate the system that the software company delivered. "}], "type": "instructions"}, {"contents": [{"type": "group_name", "content": "Take Away"}], "type": "group"}, {"type": "feedback", "content": {"attempt_feedback": [{"type": "text", "content": ""}, {"type": "text", "content": ""}], "correct_feedback": "Correct!", "incorrect_feedback": [{"type": "text", "content": "Whoops! Something important is missing."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Maybe next time..."}], "allowed_attempts": 2}}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "Instructions: Complete the following steps. Fill in the Self-Assessment."}], "type": "post_instructions"}, {"contents": [{"type": "skill", "content": "Reading"}, {"type": "skill", "content": "Speaking"}, {"type": "skill", "content": "Writing"}], "type": "learning_skills"}], "id": 11}], "stimuli": [{"_data": [], "id": 0, "contents": [{}], "type": "welcome", "template_override": 1}, {"template_override": 1, "contents": [{"value": {"video_src": "enpe8n5le02ob07re2vid01", "images": [{"time": "100", "image": "", "id": 0, "text": "<span class=\"strong\">Teacher:</span> This is your oral test for the systems program. You will answer three different questions about this term's topics and you are going to have one minute to answer each one of them. <br/>"}, {"time": "8000", "image": "", "id": 1, "text": "<span class=\"strong\">Brienne:</span> I'd rather not look at the time. I'll just focus on answering. <br/>"}, {"time": "11000", "image": "", "id": 2, "text": "<span class=\"strong\">Teacher:</span> Can you define what validation is? <br/>"}, {"time": "13000", "image": "", "id": 3, "text": "<span class=\"strong\">Brienne:</span> Sure, in the systems field, we'll always have to carry out data validation processes. I would rather not see it as a validation but as an inspection of the data needed for the system to perform suitably. This process makes sure that the different inputs of the system work in accordance with their purpose; furthermore, we would rather not execute it when the application is finished, but throughout its development stage. <br/>"}, {"time": "40000", "image": "", "id": 4, "text": "<span class=\"strong\">Teacher:</span> Can you please describe the importance of this process?<br/>"}, {"time": "43000", "image": "", "id": 5, "text": "<span class=\"strong\">Brienne: </span>Sure, the data validation is going to aim to verify the completeness and correctness of all the data needed in the application, ensuring its correct operation once it is launched. Any person who performs this process would rather not focus on the application, but on the faulty data elements to fix them right away. Furthermore, it enables an early analysis of how the application is being developed, avoiding future data loss."}, {"time": "71000", "image": "", "id": 6, "text": "<br/><span class=\"strong\">Teacher:</span> That is right. Can you describe the different options available to perform a data validation process?<br/>"}, {"time": "76000", "image": "", "id": 7, "text": "<span class=\"strong\">Brienne:</span> I would rather not be so specific about that; however, we have four different options I'm applying once I graduate.  The default validation, which identifies orphan pages and updates them; the full validation, which confirms, reports, and updates corrupted structures. The read-only validation only reports flaws, but does not fix them; finally, the ignore checksum error enables the validation of corrupted databases. <br/>"}]}, "type": "video"}], "type": "video", "_data": [], "id": 3, "title": ""}], "type": "scholar", "_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "has_nav", "content": true}, {"type": "has_exercise_controls", "content": true}], "type": "lab_options"}], "id": 0}]}